question_text:
The following change is made to `pkg/storage/tsdb/indexcache/cache.go` in the `grafana/mimir` repository:

A new method is appended to the `IndexCache` interface:

```go
// Before (final two methods of the interface)
	// StoreLabelValues stores the result of a LabelValues() call.
	StoreLabelValues(userID string, blockID ulid.ULID, labelName string, matchersKey LabelMatchersKey, v []byte)
	// FetchLabelValues fetches the result of a LabelValues() call.
	FetchLabelValues(ctx context.Context, userID string, blockID ulid.ULID, labelName string, matchersKey LabelMatchersKey) ([]byte, bool)
}

// After
	// StoreLabelValues stores the result of a LabelValues() call.
	StoreLabelValues(userID string, blockID ulid.ULID, labelName string, matchersKey LabelMatchersKey, v []byte)
	// FetchLabelValues fetches the result of a LabelValues() call.
	FetchLabelValues(ctx context.Context, userID string, blockID ulid.ULID, labelName string, matchersKey LabelMatchersKey) ([]byte, bool)

	// DeleteBlock removes all cache entries associated with the given block.
	DeleteBlock(ctx context.Context, userID string, blockID ulid.ULID) error
}
```

The new `DeleteBlock` method must be implemented by every concrete type that satisfies the `indexcache.IndexCache` interface. No other files are changed.

Which files within the `grafana/mimir` repository would fail to compile as a result of this change? List each file by its path relative to the repository root.
